---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import PageHero from '../components/PageHero.astro';
import CTA from '../components/CTA.astro';
---

<BaseLayout title="Business AI Solutions | Archytum" description="Human-approved Microsoft 365 workflow systems for small and growing businesses.">
  <PageHero eyebrow="Business AI Solutions" title="Turn daily activity into a reliable action system." lede="For small and growing businesses that need fewer dropped follow-ups, better meeting preparation, and a clearer operating rhythm—without handing control to an autonomous bot." />

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container grid-2">
      <div class="section-heading">
        <p class="eyebrow">The operating problem</p>
        <h2>Your inbox and calendar contain work. They do not organize it for you.</h2>
      </div>
      <div>
        <p>Customer requests, promised follow-ups, meeting preparation, and deadlines are scattered across threads, invites, and memory. Archytum builds a bounded command center that identifies the work, prepares the next step, and keeps external action under human approval.</p>
        <ul class="checklist">
          <li>Start each weekday with one prioritized brief</li>
          <li>See commitments, conflicts, and preparation needs</li>
          <li>Review drafts before anything leaves the business</li>
          <li>Keep source evidence and uncertainty visible</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section alt">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="section-heading">
        <p class="eyebrow">Required first paid step</p>
        <h2>Workflow Control Assessment</h2>
        <p>A five-business-day assessment that maps the current workflow, defines boundaries, and produces a fixed-scope implementation proposal.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="grid-3">
        <article class="card"><h3>Understand</h3><p>Owner interview, users and systems inventory, current-state workflow, failure points, and baseline measures.</p></article>
        <article class="card"><h3>Control</h3><p>Privacy, retention, permissions, prioritization, human approvals, and safe failure behavior.</p></article>
        <article class="card"><h3>Plan</h3><p>Target workflow, 30/60/90-day roadmap, findings session, and implementation proposal.</p></article>
      </div>
      <p class="notice"><strong>Fixed price: $1,500</strong> No production access or implementation is included. Founding-client discounts, when available, are offered privately.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="section-heading">
        <p class="eyebrow">Monthly packages</p>
        <h2>Begin with one owner. Expand only when the workflow works.</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="grid-3">
        <article class="card">
          <span class="tag">Focused</span>
          <h3>Inbox Control</h3>
          <p class="price">$1,000 <small>/ month</small></p>
          <ul class="checklist">
            <li>One Microsoft 365 user</li>
            <li>One mailbox and calendar</li>
            <li>Weekday action brief</li>
            <li>Meeting preparation and draft responses</li>
            <li>Monthly report and review</li>
            <li>Two optimization hours</li>
          </ul>
        </article>
        <article class="card featured">
          <span class="tag">Recommended</span>
          <h3>Operations Command Center</h3>
          <p class="price">$2,000 <small>/ month</small></p>
          <ul class="checklist">
            <li>Up to three approved users</li>
            <li>Up to three mailboxes and calendars</li>
            <li>One shared mailbox</li>
            <li>Team actions and pipeline follow-up</li>
            <li>Weekly operating review</li>
            <li>Six optimization hours</li>
          </ul>
        </article>
        <article class="card">
          <span class="tag">Expanded</span>
          <h3>Growth Operations</h3>
          <p class="price">$3,500 <small>/ month</small></p>
          <ul class="checklist">
            <li>Up to five approved users</li>
            <li>Two shared mailboxes</li>
            <li>Approved prospect research</li>
            <li>Outreach and post drafts</li>
            <li>Growth reporting and weekly strategy</li>
            <li>Ten optimization hours</li>
          </ul>
        </article>
      </div>
      <p class="notice"><strong>Assessment and onboarding are required and priced separately.</strong> Final scope and pricing are confirmed in writing before work begins. Third-party service and model costs are not included.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section alt">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="section-heading">
        <p class="eyebrow">Package comparison</p>
        <h2>Know what expands—and what never becomes automatic.</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="comparison-wrap" tabindex="0" aria-label="Scrollable package comparison">
        <table class="comparison">
          <thead><tr><th scope="col">Capability</th><th scope="col">Inbox Control</th><th scope="col">Command Center</th><th scope="col">Growth Operations</th></tr></thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr><td>Approved users</td><td>1</td><td>Up to 3</td><td>Up to 5</td></tr>
            <tr><td>Mailboxes/calendars</td><td>1 / 1</td><td>Up to 3 / 3</td><td>Scoped after assessment</td></tr>
            <tr><td>Weekday action brief</td><td>Included</td><td>Included</td><td>Included</td></tr>
            <tr><td>Team action and pipeline view</td><td>—</td><td>Included</td><td>Included</td></tr>
            <tr><td>Growth research and drafts</td><td>—</td><td>—</td><td>Included with limits</td></tr>
            <tr><td>Monthly optimization hours</td><td>2</td><td>6</td><td>10</td></tr>
            <tr><td>Automatic sending or posting</td><td>Never</td><td>Never</td><td>Never</td></tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container grid-2">
      <div class="section-heading"><p class="eyebrow">Fit</p><h2>This is a good fit when…</h2></div>
      <div>
        <ul class="checklist">
          <li>Important work is buried in Outlook and Calendar</li>
          <li>A small leadership team still manages follow-up personally</li>
          <li>You want better preparation without unattended external actions</li>
          <li>You can name the workflow, owner, and desired outcome</li>
        </ul>
        <p>It is not a fit for unlimited virtual-assistant work, mass outreach, autonomous sending, emergency support, or safety-critical decisions.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <CTA eyebrow="Business AI Fit Call" title="See whether your workflow is ready for a command center." text="Complete the short Business AI intake. If the request is a fit, Archytum will coordinate a free 25-minute call by email." primaryLabel="Start the Business AI intake" primaryHref="/contact/?path=business" />
</BaseLayout>
